config BR2_PACKAGE_LUAJIT_EMBED
	bool "luajit-embed"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_LUAJIT_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS # dlopen
	help
	  LuaJIT built as an embeddable library rather than as the
	  system Lua interpreter.

	  Buildroot's luajit package registers itself as the provider
	  of the "luainterpreter" virtual package and symlinks
	  /usr/bin/lua to itself, so it cannot coexist with lua - the
	  build stops with a configuration error if both are selected.
	  That is a problem for this image, which needs both:
	  WirePlumber requires the Lua 5.4 ABI, while love and
	  solarus-engine require the LuaJIT (Lua 5.1) API.

	  This package builds the same sources and installs the
	  library, headers and the luajit binary, but claims neither
	  the virtual package nor the /usr/bin/lua name. Engines link
	  it directly; lua stays the system interpreter.

	  https://luajit.org
